["17:36"]={
{"At that moment I looked again at my watch because I wanted to be back at the Cathedral as Evensong ended at about twenty to six in order to talk to the choirmaster before he left. I saw I only had four minutes before it ended.\n“So that occurred at \003precisely twenty-four minutes before six\004?”\n“Exactly.”","The Unburied","Charles Palliser",true},
},
["17:37"]={
{"Look, Lucille, said Joe when Lucille strolled into the office at \0035:37\004. “I don’t know what you said to this gal, but it seems to have had exactly the opposite of the desired effect. She’s got some bee in her bonnet about Harvard Law School.”","Lightning Rods","Helen DeWitt",true},
},
["17:38"]={
{"And then I see something I recognise. Some little green digits, glowing in the blackness. It’s Ben’s alarm clock. Somehow I’m back here, in the apartment. I blink the numbers. \00317:38\004. But that can’t be right. That’s the afternoon.","The Paris Apartment","Lucy Foley",true},
{"He stares at the phone, thinks: Ring. Ring now. But it remains inert. \0035:38 p.m.\004 Bunny will be done with her housekeeping shift by now.","Cloud Cuckoo Land","Anthony Doerr",true},
{"It was \0035:38 p.m.\004 when the Prime Minister’s plane finally broke through the clouds and appeared above Heston Aerodrome. As the ground flickered into view, Legat could see the traffic along the Great West Road. Cars were halted for more than a mile in either direction. It had been raining heavily.","Munich","Robert Harris",true},
},
["17:39"]={
{"It’s \00305:39\004 so we can have dinner, it’s quick noodles. While they’re in the hot water, Ma finds hard words to test me from the milk carton like nutritional that means food, and pasteurized that means laser guns zapped away the germs.","Room","Emma Donoghue",true},
},
["17:40"]={
{"As no one had “any other business” to raise, I closed the meeting at \0035:40\004, and suggested to Jeremy that he join Rosemary and me for dinner. I wanted to see them together.","Trial and Error","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"What? I said, “is it 5:30 yet?”\n“Er, \0035:40\004.” Heavens, they’ll be starving. But then that’s a good thing. Let them.","I Love Dollars","Zhu Wen",true},
},
["17:41"]={
{"All right, people, let’s haul ass. Sunset’s at \00317:41\004 and we’ve got twenty-three k to go. Staff Segeant Beyn got to his feet and the platoon followed.","The Heart of Valor","Tanya Huff",false},
},
["17:42"]={
{"Well, they set sail, and after going ever so many thousand miles, or hundred — I forget which, but it doesn’t matter — a great storm arose, a typhoon or simoon, perhaps both; and after slowly gathering up its energies for the space of twenty-nine days, seven hours, and twenty-three minutes, without counting the seconds, it burst upon them at exactly \003forty-two minutes past five\004, on the sixth day of the week.","The Dodge Club; Or, Italy in MDCCCLIX","James De Mille",true},
},
["17:43"]={
{"“I always prefer to travel on a British carrier,” Don Pedro told the purser as they were shown to their seats in first class. The Boeing Stratocruiser took off at \0035:43 p.m.\004, just a few minutes behind schedule.","Best Kept Secret","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"It’s \0035:43\004. Time is racing, racing.","If It Bleeds","Stephen King",true},
},
["17:44"]={
{"Janice is not waiting for him in the lounge or beside the pool when at last \003around 5:45\004 they come home from playing the par-5 eighteenth. Instead one of the girls in their green and white uniforms comes over and tells him that his wife wants him to call home.","Rabbit Is Rich","John Updike",true},
},
["17:45"]={
{"“A \003quarter to six\004,” answered the midwife.\n“And what if I really am dying?” thought Olga Mihalovna, looking at her husband’s head and the window-panes on which the rain was beating.","The Party","Anton Pavlovich Chekhov",true},
{"At \003a quarter to six\004, there was a rapping sound outside my door. I checked out the peephole. Ramirez stood outside, dressed in a big red basketball-type tank top, black shorts, and flip-flops.","White Night","Jim Butcher",true},
},
["17:46"]={
{"At \003fourteen minutes to six\004 they walked into the director’s study, where a young lady of Sally’s age offered the guests a choice of dry sherry or orange juice.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer",true},
},
["17:47"]={
{"Then I take it the matter is practically concluded, said the clergyman. “And that you very properly submit to return to your proper home. And now, if I may offer a suggestion, it is that we take tea. Freed of its tannin, nothing, I think, is more refreshing and stimulating.”\n“There’s a train from Lyndhurst at \003thirteen minutes to six\004,” said Widgery, unfolding a time table.","The Wheels of Chance: A Bicycling Idyll","H.G. Wells",true},
},
["17:48"]={
{"Father came home at \0035:48 p.m.\004 I heard him come through the front door. Then he came into the living room. He was wearing a lime green and sky blue check shirt and there was a double knot on one of his shoes but not on the other.","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon",true},
},
["17:49"]={
{"\0035:49 P.M.\004, SUNDAY, JUNE 8TH, 1924 WHEN ODELL ARRIVED back at Camp IV, he was unable to conceal his excitement. He crawled into Norton’s tent and told him what he’d seen.","Paths of Glory","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"It was \003eleven minutes to six\004. After a moment he idly drew the center drawer of the desk out over his lap. For a moment he stared at the gun without recognition. Then he gave a yelp and leaped up. She had put it back!","The Comforts of Home","Flannery O’Connor",true},
},
["17:50"]={
{"He glanced up at the clock above the door: \003ten to six\004. Young Kevin would appear through that door at any moment and ask if he would be kind enough to move on.","The Grass is Always Greener","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"What time is it Jack?\n“\003Ten to six\004”\n“Ten more minutes then.” I shuffle the cards. “Time for a quick game of rummy?”","Noughts and Crosses","Malorie Blackman",true},
{"Esterville had called the truck stop, but no one had seen his wife come in. She hadn’t returned home. Cork and McDougal found her red Mustang at \0035:50\004.","Corpus Delicti","William Kent Krueger",true},
},
["17:51"]={
{"She read through the first page slowly and made of a couple of emendations, aware that any mistake made hastily on a Friday evening could be regretted in the weeks to come. She glanced at the clock on her desk as she signed the final page of the document. It was just showing \0035:51\004.","Never Stop on the Motorway","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"The sun was red and the shadows were long and dark. It wanted but \003nine minutes to six\004, and within the hotel the disgraceful National Swill was in full flow, men pouring as much liquor down their throats as possible before the fatal hour of drought arrived.","Venom House","Arthur Upfield",true},
},
["17:52"]={
{"It was \003eight minutes to six o’clock\004. “I must get him,” he told the telephone girl for the dozenth time.\n“Sorry— no one will answer,” she said wearily.","Jimmy Kirkland and the Plot for a Pennant","Hugh S. Fullerton",true},
},
["17:53"]={
{"That boy will be spoiled, as sure as I go on springs; he’s made such a lot of. Have you been regulated?\n“I should think I have!” exclaimed I, in indignant recollection of my education.\n“All right; keep your temper. What time are you?”\n“\003Seven minutes to six\004.”","The Adventures of a Three-Guinea Watch","Talbot Baines Reed",true},
},
["17:54"]={
{"It was \0035:54 p.m.\004 when Father came back into the living room. He said, “What is this?” but he said it very quietly and I didn’t realise that he was angry because he wasn’t shouting.","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon",true},
},
["17:55"]={
{"One, two, three, four, five, six… She wound each clock in turn, three turns each, putting just enough power in the springs to get them ticking in time for Mr Westcott’s inspection. Speaking of which…it was \003five minutes to six\004. Five minutes before Mr. Westcott would arrive to inspect his clocks. Helena swallowed. She could hear footsteps thundering in the room below and the occasional exclamation from Stanley.","The House of One Hundred Clocks","A.M. Howell",true},
{"The wind moaned and sang dismally, catching the ears and lifting the shabby coat-tails of Mr. Mortimer Jenkyn, ‘Photographic Artist’, as he stood outside and put the shutters up with this own cold hands in despair of further trade. It was \003five minutes to six\004.","The Deferred Appointment","Algernon Blackwood",true},
},
["17:56"]={
{"Now, sir, the hand wants \003four minutes to six\004. If the hour strike before you call yourself a wanton, gratuitous calumniator, I’ll flog you round the room.","The Knight of Gwynne","Charles James Lever",true},
},
["17:57"]={
{"At \003three minutes to six\004, despite there still being no sign of Sally, the director suggested they should all make their way to the Great Hall.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"At \003three minutes to six\004, a tall, well-built man of military bearing pushed his way through the revolving doors. His dark navy blazer, gray flannels, short hair and highly polished shoes all suggested a life of discipline.","Only Time Will Tell","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"Hugo Carmody had done this, with the result that by \003three minutes to six\004 he was feeling as if he had been marooned among roses since the beginning of summer.","Summer Lightning","P.G. Wodehouse",true},
{"He would make his way by charm, the charm of voice, of jewel-like language, above all by the intellectual charm of new, moving, luminous ideas. At \003three minutes to six\004 the doctor closed the book and waited.","The Drunkard","Guy Thorne",true},
},
["17:58"]={
{"Then I notice the windows: they’re shiny dark. \00317:58\004, insists my watch. It can’t be. It’s only just gone four. I peer around my tormentor’s belly to find Immaculée Constantin, but she’s gone.","The Bone Clocks","David Mitchell",true},
},
["17:59"]={
{"At \003one minute to six\004, the director led the guest of honor onto the stage. He watched the four hundred girls rise and applaud him in what the director would have described as a “ladylike” manner.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"It was \003nearly six o’clock\004 in the evening, and the absurd bell in the six-foot tin steeple of the church went clank-clank, clank- clank! as old Mattu pulled the rope within.","Burmese Days","George Orwell",true},
{"When he arrived it was \003nearly six o’clock\004, and the sun was setting full and warm, and the red light streamed in through the window and gave more colour to the pale cheeks.","Dracula","Bram Stoker",true},
},
}
